      "body": "Hi maintainers, would like to take this. Two clarifying questions before I open a PR:\n\n1. For the link, prefer pinning to a tagged release (e.g. \\`pytest-xdist\\` v3.x) over \\`main\\`? Tagged feels safer against doc drift.\n2. Worth updating the example to use the \\`@pytest.hookspec\\` decorator inline, since that matches current \\`pytest-xdist/src/xdist/newhooks.py\\` style? Or keep the doc minimal and only fix the link?\n\nHappy to scope to just (1) if (2) is out of scope for a docs fix.\n",
